“I began working with Jairo in the 1980s,” said Henry Cárdenas , CEO of CMN, in a statement. “I am extremely happy to continue this great work and this partnership with Grupo Niche, which began in the ’80s alongside our great composer and group director, Jairo Varela. For me, having them as part of CMN’s portfolio is a way to continue honoring his legacy. I am honored to stand alongside this great group, which is not only Colombian, but represents a genre with global reach.”&nbsp;

Known for classic salsa tunes such as “Una Aventura,” “Gotas de Lluvia” and “Mi Pueblo,” Grupo Niche was founded in 1978 by the late Jairo Varela in Santiago de Cali — the third-most populous city in Colombia after Bogotá and Medellín — also known as “La capital mundial de la salsa” (the salsa capital of the world). One of the group’s most notable songs is “Cali Pachanguero,” which celebrated its 40th anniversary in 2024 and still resonates with proud Colombians everywhere.&nbsp;

On Billboard &#8216;s Top Tropical Albums chart, the group has 19 entries, including seven top 10 titles. On the Tropical Airplay chart, it has placed 11 songs, three of them in the top 10. Over its career, the group has won two Latin Grammys and one Grammy.
